# command: make -C micro run
# build: make -C micro all
# cwd: repository root
# exit code: 0
# note: OpenSBI banner omitted; NUL padding from OpenSBI removed with `tr -d '\000'`.
# note: real QEMU virt, not a host-side function-call demo. The run was wrapped in
#       `timeout 25s`; rc=0 means the kernel shut QEMU down, not timeout 124.
# note: default BOOT_MODULES=capability. After [capability] PASS, bootstrap arms a
#       1 ms SBI timer and runs two kernel workers through shared/demo.c's unified
#       trap glue. The probe rebuilds object/sched state around its own static
#       probe_runner; it does not reuse capability run()'s stack-local current.
# note: decisive evidence is worker-b starting before worker-a is done plus both
#       workers resuming after a timer switch. Tick/switch/quantum counters are
#       corroborating values, not proof by themselves.
# note: this probe is a boot verification-only exception; boot itself still does
#       not create the first user/service thread.

